Template: jaiabot-embedded/debconf_state_common
Type: select
Choices: type, fleet_id, led_type, electronics_stack, comms_links, mode, warp, rf_encryption_password, dccl_encryption_password, NEXT
Description: Choose a common option to edit

Template: jaiabot-embedded/debconf_state_bot
Type: select
Choices: BACK, bot_id, arduino_type, pam_connection_type, imu_type, bot_type, data_offload_ignore_type, imu_install_type, temperature_sensor_type, pressure_sensor_type, motor_harness_type, camera_positions, additional_sensors, EXIT
Description: Choose a bot option to edit

Template: jaiabot-embedded/debconf_state_hub
Type: select
Choices: BACK, hub_id, user_role, EXIT
Description: Choose a hub option to edit

Template: jaiabot-embedded/type
Type: select
Choices: bot, hub
Description: Is this a bot or a hub?
  This choice will determine which applications will be configured to launch with systemd.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/mode
Type: select
Choices: runtime, simulation
Default: runtime
Description: Is this bot or hub to be run in runtime (operational) or simulation mode?
  This choice will determine which applications will be configured to launch with systemd.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/warp
Type: select
Choices: 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 30, 40, 50
Default: 1
Description: At what multiple of real speed should this simulation be run?
  A value of 1 is normal speed, 10 is 10x the real clock, etc.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/bot_id
Type: string
Default: 0
Description: Bot identification number
  This is used to set the hostname of the computer and set the correct value in the jaiabot configuration.
  Valid bot_ids are 0 to 150, as reported by "jaia admin bounds --bot_id".
  To change in the future, run "sudo dpkg-reconfigure jaiabot-embedded"

Template: jaiabot-embedded/bot_id_invalid
Type: error
Description: Invalid bot identification number
  The bot_id must be a whole number in the range reported by
  "jaia admin bounds --bot_id". Please enter one in that range.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/hub_id
Type: string
Default: 0
Description: Hub identification number
  This is used to set the hostname of the computer and set the correct value in the jaiabot configuration.
  Valid hub_ids are 0 to 30, as reported by "jaia admin bounds --hub_id".
  To change in the future, run "sudo dpkg-reconfigure jaiabot-embedded"

Template: jaiabot-embedded/hub_id_invalid
Type: error
Description: Invalid hub identification number
  The hub_id must be a whole number in the range reported by
  "jaia admin bounds --hub_id". Please enter one in that range.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/fleet_id
Type: string
Default: 0
Description: Fleet identification number
  This is used to set the correct value in the jaiabot configuration.
  Valid fleet ids are 0 to 4000, as reported by "jaia admin bounds --fleet_id";
  those above 250 are addressed with IPv6 rather than IPv4.
  To change in the future, run "sudo dpkg-reconfigure jaiabot-embedded"

Template: jaiabot-embedded/fleet_id_invalid
Type: error
Description: Invalid fleet identification number
  The fleet id must be a whole number in the range reported by
  "jaia admin bounds --fleet_id". Please enter one in that range.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/arduino_type
Type: select
Default: none
Choices: spi, usb, none
Description: What type of Arduino connection does this bot have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/pam_connection_type
Type: select
Default: none
Choices: uart, usb, none
Description: What type of PAM connection does this bot have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/led_type
Type: select
Choices: hub_led, none
Default: none
Description: What type of leds does your system have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/electronics_stack
Type: select
Choices: 0, 1, 2
Default: 0
Description: What type of electronics stack do you have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/user_role
Type: select
Choices: user, advanced, developer
Default: user
Description: The user role to be set in the Upgrade UI (this sets which Ansible playbooks are visible to the user).

Template: jaiabot-embedded/imu_type
Type: select
Choices: bno055, bno085, none
Default: bno055
Description: What type of imu does your system have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/bot_type
Type: select
Choices: hydro, pam, bio, none
Default: hydro
Description: What type of bot is your system?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/data_offload_ignore_type
Type: select
Choices: goby, taskpacket, none
Default: none
Description: What data types to ignore when sending data to the hub?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/imu_install_type
Type: select
Choices: embedded, retrofit, none
Default: embedded
Description: What type of imu installation does your system have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/motor_harness_type
Type: select
Choices: rpm_and_thermistor, none
Default: none
Description: What type of motor harness does your bot have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/temperature_sensor_type
Type: select
Choices: bar02, bar30, tsys01, none
Default: bar30
Description: What temperature sensor do you want to use?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/pressure_sensor_type
Type: select
Choices: bar02, bar30, none
Default: bar30
Description: What pressure sensor do you have?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/rf_encryption_password
Type: string
Default:
Description: Encryption key for XBee radio: 128-bit value (up to 16 bytes) as hex

Template: jaiabot-embedded/comms_links
Type: multiselect
Choices: xbee, wifi, iridium
Default: xbee
Description: Which comms links to activate?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/camera_positions
Type: multiselect
Choices: aft, fore, outward, none
Default: none
Description: Which camera positions?

Template: jaiabot-embedded/dccl_encryption_password
Type: string
Default:
Description: Encryption passphrase for DCCL (intervehicle) messages: can be any string.

Template: jaiabot-embedded/additional_sensors
Type: multiselect
Choices: turner_c_flour, aml, ppk, none
Default: none
Description: Which additional sensors?
